# 5. Multiple Values in Match

We can use `|` to match multiple values.

```python
day = "Saturday"

match day:
    case "Saturday" | "Sunday":
        print("Weekend")
    case "Monday" | "Tuesday" | "Wednesday" | "Thursday" | "Friday":
        print("Weekday")
    case _:
        print("Invalid day")
```

### Output

```text
Weekend
```

Here:

```python
case "Saturday" | "Sunday":
```

means either `"Saturday"` OR `"Sunday"`.

