# 8. Why Use Match?

`match` can make code easier to understand when you have many fixed choices or patterns.

### Without Match

```python
command = "start"

if command == "start":
    print("Starting...")
elif command == "stop":
    print("Stopping...")
elif command == "restart":
    print("Restarting...")
else:
    print("Unknown command")
```

### With Match

```python
command = "start"

match command:
    case "start":
        print("Starting...")
    case "stop":
        print("Stopping...")
    case "restart":
        print("Restarting...")
    case _:
        print("Unknown command")
```

Both can solve the same problem.

